1
00:00:03,625 --> 00:00:06,227
[SPEAKER_02]: You were born here in Napa or Napa?

2
00:00:06,267 --> 00:00:07,147
[SPEAKER_01]: Napa.

3
00:00:07,588 --> 00:00:10,069
[SPEAKER_02]: In January 16th, 1894?

4
00:00:10,149 --> 00:00:10,289
[SPEAKER_02]: 95.

5
00:00:10,509 --> 00:00:12,831
[SPEAKER_02]: Record book says 94, huh?

6
00:00:12,931 --> 00:00:13,431
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, right.

7
00:00:13,471 --> 00:00:15,192
[SPEAKER_02]: 83, right?

8
00:00:15,252 --> 00:00:16,713
[SPEAKER_01]: 83, yeah.

9
00:00:17,153 --> 00:00:20,335
[SPEAKER_01]: 83 left, yeah.

10
00:00:22,897 --> 00:00:24,338
[SPEAKER_02]: Did your family always live here?

11
00:00:24,358 --> 00:00:24,938
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, yes.

12
00:00:25,198 --> 00:00:26,379
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, they all lived here.

13
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,121
[SPEAKER_02]: And did your father play ball?

14
00:00:29,341 --> 00:00:29,721
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

15
00:00:30,582 --> 00:00:31,342
[SPEAKER_02]: He was a farmer.

16
00:00:31,762 --> 00:00:32,223
[SPEAKER_02]: I see.

17
00:00:35,742 --> 00:00:38,123
[SPEAKER_02]: Where did his father come from?

18
00:00:38,224 --> 00:00:39,024
[SPEAKER_02]: Someplace else?

19
00:00:39,104 --> 00:00:39,404
[SPEAKER_01]: Italy.

20
00:00:39,444 --> 00:00:40,265
[SPEAKER_01]: He came from Italy.

21
00:00:40,325 --> 00:00:40,805
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, he was?

22
00:00:40,885 --> 00:00:41,946
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, I see.

23
00:00:41,986 --> 00:00:43,427
[SPEAKER_02]: How'd he happen to settle out here, I wonder?

24
00:00:44,327 --> 00:00:48,830
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, this is a wine country, you know, and there's a lot of Italians settled here from Italy.

25
00:00:49,170 --> 00:00:50,171
[SPEAKER_01]: Lots of them.

26
00:00:51,091 --> 00:00:54,974
[SPEAKER_01]: And you'll find, if you look through the phone book, you'll see a lot of Italian names.

27
00:00:55,214 --> 00:00:56,615
[SPEAKER_01]: Fourth and fifth generation.

28
00:00:57,455 --> 00:00:57,735
[SPEAKER_00]: Now.

29
00:00:58,035 --> 00:01:02,078
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the time they used to have gold.

30
00:01:03,487 --> 00:01:10,489
[SPEAKER_01]: At least I can think of five hotels that are run by Italian, poor Italian people.

31
00:01:10,969 --> 00:01:15,890
[SPEAKER_01]: They work in the vineyards and the fruits and the canneries.

32
00:01:16,170 --> 00:01:17,271
[SPEAKER_02]: Where'd you first play ball?

33
00:01:17,391 --> 00:01:19,091
[SPEAKER_02]: You had a sandlot ball around here?

34
00:01:19,431 --> 00:01:20,152
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh yeah, right here.

35
00:01:20,172 --> 00:01:21,072
[SPEAKER_01]: We had a little team.

36
00:01:22,212 --> 00:01:25,753
[SPEAKER_01]: They called the Alpa Heights.

37
00:01:27,413 --> 00:01:29,474
[SPEAKER_01]: We used to play the St. Louis...

38
00:01:30,614 --> 00:01:32,935
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, a form of the St. Helena.

39
00:01:34,246 --> 00:01:36,168
[SPEAKER_01]: And Dutch Juni was one of them.

40
00:01:36,208 --> 00:01:38,971
[SPEAKER_01]: He was also a ballplayer professional.

41
00:01:39,592 --> 00:01:41,534
[SPEAKER_01]: Juni, J-U-N-I-Y.

42
00:01:41,554 --> 00:01:42,375
[SPEAKER_01]: He's dead now.

43
00:01:42,415 --> 00:01:43,817
[SPEAKER_01]: He's been gone quite a while.

44
00:01:43,857 --> 00:01:51,085
[SPEAKER_01]: He had us around 19... 6 and 7 and 8.

45
00:01:51,105 --> 00:01:52,486
[SPEAKER_02]: He was a kid.

46
00:01:52,506 --> 00:01:53,988
[SPEAKER_02]: What position did you play in those days?

47
00:01:54,008 --> 00:01:55,309
[SPEAKER_01]: First base, always first base.

48
00:01:57,332 --> 00:01:58,933
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you have a high school here at Napa you went to?

49
00:01:58,953 --> 00:01:59,193
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, yeah.

50
00:01:59,273 --> 00:02:00,494
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you play on the team there?

51
00:02:00,514 --> 00:02:04,315
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, I got caught without a mask one day and that finished me in third catchment.

52
00:02:04,335 --> 00:02:05,155
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, what happened?

53
00:02:05,196 --> 00:02:06,036
[SPEAKER_01]: I got hit in the eye.

54
00:02:06,556 --> 00:02:07,456
[SPEAKER_01]: Why didn't you have a mask on?

55
00:02:07,476 --> 00:02:08,377
[SPEAKER_01]: We didn't have any masks.

56
00:02:08,437 --> 00:02:08,997
[SPEAKER_01]: Is that right?

57
00:02:09,057 --> 00:02:10,258
[SPEAKER_01]: We didn't have any.

58
00:02:10,298 --> 00:02:13,279
[SPEAKER_01]: Or at least if they forgot it, I don't know.

59
00:02:14,079 --> 00:02:15,400
[SPEAKER_02]: And you went on to St. Mary's, right?

60
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:16,680
[SPEAKER_02]: St. Mary's, yeah.

61
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:18,801
[SPEAKER_01]: What did you plan to do at St. Mary's?

62
00:02:18,821 --> 00:02:19,822
[SPEAKER_01]: What was your major field?

63
00:02:19,842 --> 00:02:20,822
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you have anything in particular?

64
00:02:20,842 --> 00:02:22,863
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I was in the banking at St. Mary's.

65
00:02:23,183 --> 00:02:25,444
[SPEAKER_01]: I had a course there, a banking course.

66
00:02:26,488 --> 00:02:28,229
[SPEAKER_01]: Except that, and then I went into baseball.

67
00:02:28,289 --> 00:02:31,149
[SPEAKER_02]: They had a pretty good team there, didn't they?

68
00:02:31,169 --> 00:02:31,930
[SPEAKER_01]: They might, yeah.

69
00:02:32,390 --> 00:02:33,670
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, they had a pretty good team.

70
00:02:34,410 --> 00:02:36,771
[SPEAKER_01]: We used to play the Coast League during spring training.

71
00:02:36,931 --> 00:02:39,872
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you ever beat them?

72
00:02:40,372 --> 00:02:41,072
[SPEAKER_01]: Once in a while.

73
00:02:41,112 --> 00:02:50,135
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't think we ever did while I was playing, but the team before me did, and they had some pretty good players, like Tiny Leonard and Dutch Leonard.

74
00:02:50,715 --> 00:02:51,716
[SPEAKER_01]: Dutch Leonard, okay.

75
00:02:51,736 --> 00:02:51,916
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

76
00:02:53,296 --> 00:02:55,817
[SPEAKER_01]: In fact, they beat the Red Sox at 2-1.

77
00:02:56,820 --> 00:02:57,961
[SPEAKER_01]: They keep giving two to one.

78
00:02:58,121 --> 00:03:01,244
[SPEAKER_01]: They come out and they were training out here.

79
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:06,189
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you play ball all year round out here in the good weather or most of the year?

80
00:03:06,209 --> 00:03:08,330
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, most of the year we played.

81
00:03:08,390 --> 00:03:11,613
[SPEAKER_01]: I noticed in the recent draft judges, so many of them come from the west coast.

82
00:03:11,633 --> 00:03:12,354
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, yeah.

83
00:03:12,494 --> 00:03:14,396
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, sure.

84
00:03:14,436 --> 00:03:17,218
[SPEAKER_01]: The weather is so, you know, you can play most of the year, every day.

85
00:03:17,679 --> 00:03:19,921
[SPEAKER_02]: What year did you finish up at St. Mary's then?

86
00:03:21,302 --> 00:03:23,304
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, that was... 1915 or something?

87
00:03:24,397 --> 00:03:24,957
[SPEAKER_01]: What do you mean?

88
00:03:25,258 --> 00:03:25,658
[SPEAKER_01]: Sixteen.

89
00:03:25,938 --> 00:03:26,478
[SPEAKER_01]: Sixteen?

90
00:03:26,578 --> 00:03:27,359
[SPEAKER_01]: Congratulations.

91
00:03:27,419 --> 00:03:27,819
[SPEAKER_01]: Sixteen.

92
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:31,101
[SPEAKER_01]: And who signed you for Cleveland?

93
00:03:31,121 --> 00:03:32,802
[SPEAKER_01]: Two of the students at St. Mary's.

94
00:03:33,262 --> 00:03:34,863
[SPEAKER_01]: Not for Cleveland, but for Portland.

95
00:03:34,883 --> 00:03:36,484
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why I started with Portland.

96
00:03:37,305 --> 00:03:41,367
[SPEAKER_01]: Cleveland, Mr. Bernard, he was the vice president of Cleveland.

97
00:03:41,387 --> 00:03:44,970
[SPEAKER_01]: He signed me for him.

98
00:03:45,230 --> 00:03:45,790
[SPEAKER_01]: To see you?

99
00:03:46,450 --> 00:03:48,852
[SPEAKER_01]: No, to see the managers of the Portland club.

100
00:03:49,372 --> 00:03:50,733
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't know anything about it.

101
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:52,194
[SPEAKER_02]: Is this McCready running Portland?

102
00:03:52,274 --> 00:03:53,375
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, Walter McCready.

103
00:03:54,856 --> 00:03:57,057
[SPEAKER_01]: His uncle, I think, was the president.

104
00:03:59,658 --> 00:04:01,879
[SPEAKER_02]: So the St. Mary's students recommended you?

105
00:04:01,899 --> 00:04:02,359
[SPEAKER_01]: Two of them.

106
00:04:02,940 --> 00:04:03,360
[SPEAKER_01]: Both of them.

107
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:05,221
[SPEAKER_02]: They're both alive, too.

108
00:04:05,321 --> 00:04:06,321
[SPEAKER_02]: Portland signed you then?

109
00:04:06,341 --> 00:04:06,681
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

110
00:04:07,261 --> 00:04:08,682
[SPEAKER_02]: And that was your first year in football?

111
00:04:08,702 --> 00:04:09,422
[SPEAKER_02]: That's the first year.

112
00:04:09,542 --> 00:04:09,843
[SPEAKER_02]: 1916?

113
00:04:09,883 --> 00:04:11,803
[SPEAKER_02]: 1916, yeah.

114
00:04:11,823 --> 00:04:14,845
[SPEAKER_02]: Was it a pretty big thrill going up there to the Coast League?

115
00:04:14,865 --> 00:04:17,446
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, I can't remember very much of it now.

116
00:04:18,906 --> 00:04:19,887
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, of course it was fun.

117
00:04:19,927 --> 00:04:24,629
[SPEAKER_01]: We were at the spring training, Sacramento III of Charlie Holliker.

118
00:04:25,498 --> 00:04:27,699
[SPEAKER_01]: Carson Bigby and myself for three years.

119
00:04:28,879 --> 00:04:32,220
[SPEAKER_01]: They didn't have very many, what they called, butchers in those days, you know.

120
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,620
[SPEAKER_01]: Just a few of us.

121
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:41,042
[SPEAKER_01]: And one of the three of us went up in the big leagues.

122
00:04:41,082 --> 00:04:42,882
[SPEAKER_01]: Holliday was the good one, too.

123
00:04:43,102 --> 00:04:43,542
[SPEAKER_02]: What happened?

124
00:04:43,582 --> 00:04:44,823
[SPEAKER_02]: He was suffering a lot with him.

125
00:04:44,843 --> 00:04:46,463
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, he just thought he was sick.

126
00:04:46,563 --> 00:04:49,324
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, he was a beautiful player.

127
00:04:49,344 --> 00:04:54,865
[SPEAKER_02]: There used to be pictures of him in the sporting news when he was just coming up, about the great future, you know.

128
00:05:01,253 --> 00:05:04,035
[SPEAKER_02]: So Bernard signed you then, is that right?

129
00:05:04,255 --> 00:05:05,216
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

130
00:05:05,256 --> 00:05:06,697
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you get much money from Cleveland?

131
00:05:07,217 --> 00:05:09,358
[SPEAKER_01]: Not very much, not very much.

132
00:05:09,378 --> 00:05:11,920
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you join the team then, the end of the season?

133
00:05:12,621 --> 00:05:17,323
[SPEAKER_01]: Not the end of the season, during the season, in August I think it was.

134
00:05:17,343 --> 00:05:18,324
[SPEAKER_01]: Met him in Chicago.

135
00:05:21,566 --> 00:05:22,607
[SPEAKER_02]: Who was their first baseman?

136
00:05:24,108 --> 00:05:24,468
[SPEAKER_01]: Gando.

137
00:05:25,024 --> 00:05:29,525
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, he just died recently.

138
00:05:29,565 --> 00:05:30,906
[SPEAKER_01]: He was in Calistoga.

139
00:05:31,526 --> 00:05:39,468
[SPEAKER_01]: His home was Berkeley, I think, originally from Berkeley.

140
00:05:41,929 --> 00:05:44,189
[SPEAKER_02]: So you got a few games?

141
00:05:44,229 --> 00:05:46,390
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, a few, not very many.

142
00:05:47,810 --> 00:05:53,112
[SPEAKER_01]: Then the war came on and

143
00:05:54,632 --> 00:05:56,052
[SPEAKER_01]: That finished it.

144
00:05:56,072 --> 00:05:57,893
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, did you go to training in 17?

145
00:05:57,933 --> 00:05:58,153
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

146
00:05:58,733 --> 00:05:59,534
[SPEAKER_01]: Down in New Orleans?

147
00:05:59,614 --> 00:06:01,014
[SPEAKER_02]: I trained in New Orleans.

148
00:06:01,714 --> 00:06:04,535
[SPEAKER_02]: You got in, it says here, about 73 games that year.

149
00:06:05,115 --> 00:06:06,156
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, something like that.

150
00:06:06,176 --> 00:06:08,136
[SPEAKER_02]: Pretty good, huh?

151
00:06:08,156 --> 00:06:10,417
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, but you got to be playing every day.

152
00:06:10,577 --> 00:06:12,117
[SPEAKER_01]: That game, you got to be playing every day.

153
00:06:12,137 --> 00:06:15,378
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't be from one day to the other, you know.

154
00:06:15,678 --> 00:06:17,119
[SPEAKER_02]: Lee Fole was managing the team tonight?

155
00:06:17,139 --> 00:06:17,699
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, Lee Fole.

156
00:06:17,719 --> 00:06:18,579
[SPEAKER_01]: How'd you like him?

157
00:06:18,739 --> 00:06:19,840
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I liked him very much.

158
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:22,140
[SPEAKER_01]: And after, Speaker was kind of a...

159
00:06:22,821 --> 00:06:23,921
[SPEAKER_01]: I guess I hear, who was it?

160
00:06:24,534 --> 00:06:32,977
[SPEAKER_02]: George Uley or somebody told me that the speaker used to really call the shots almost from center field occasionally for a fall on the bench.

161
00:06:34,317 --> 00:06:39,459
[SPEAKER_02]: Like pitcher changes, so I'd go along with the speaker.

162
00:06:40,279 --> 00:06:43,080
[SPEAKER_02]: All you had was Jack Rainey was his name?

163
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:45,241
[SPEAKER_02]: Jack Rainey was there, yeah.

164
00:06:45,401 --> 00:06:46,201
[SPEAKER_02]: Steve O'Neill.

165
00:06:47,141 --> 00:06:48,582
[SPEAKER_02]: Womby was there.

166
00:06:48,602 --> 00:06:49,722
[SPEAKER_01]: Joe Womby.

167
00:06:49,762 --> 00:06:51,803
[SPEAKER_01]: He was a faculty neighbor of ours.

168
00:06:51,823 --> 00:06:52,463
[SPEAKER_01]: Joe Sewell.

169
00:06:53,016 --> 00:06:55,797
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, Chapman was there first.

170
00:06:55,817 --> 00:06:56,497
[SPEAKER_01]: Joe Seward.

171
00:06:57,197 --> 00:06:57,817
[SPEAKER_01]: Barry Gardner.

172
00:06:58,057 --> 00:06:58,777
[SPEAKER_01]: Barry Gardner.

173
00:06:58,857 --> 00:07:00,698
[SPEAKER_01]: I was thinking about it last night.

174
00:07:00,738 --> 00:07:03,938
[SPEAKER_01]: I saw a little of the tape from the television.

175
00:07:03,978 --> 00:07:07,519
[SPEAKER_01]: When he hits a ball, he'd look at it before he threw it.

176
00:07:07,779 --> 00:07:08,199
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

177
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,440
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know what he was doing, but he'd always get it there ahead of him.

178
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:13,441
